== Principles ==
- Public binding surface is UNCHANGED. `int recv(received_t&, recv_flags_t)` and its return/parity
  contract stay identical. Only the INTERNAL fill of received_t._parts changes. No numbers
  fabrication. Match surrounding cpp style/idiom. Keep thread-safety/single-consumer.

== TASK (apply-plan step ⑤, cpp binding) ==
Replace the internal per-part receive loop that fills received_t with a SINGLE whole-message recv
call into a reusable/growable array, then move those parts into received_t._parts.

Current internals (re-verify with grep before editing):
- bindings/cpp/src/Runtime/Sockets/detail.hpp — receive-into-received helpers with recv_part loops
  (~lines 98, 124, 151 use zlink_recv_part / zlink_router_recv_part in a has_more loop).
- bindings/cpp/src/Runtime/Native/native_receive.hpp — thin wrappers over zlink_*_recv_part.
- bindings/cpp/src/Runtime/Sockets/{pair,dealer,router}.cpp — recv(received_t&) call the helpers.

Transition:
- PAIR/DEALER recv(received_t&): call zlink_recv once into a caller-owned zlink_msg_t array; fill
  received_t (no routing id). ROUTER recv(received_t&): call zlink_router_recv once; fill parts +
  routing_id + reply token.
- Capacity: use a growable buffer (e.g. a std::vector<message_t>/raw zlink_msg_t array the socket or
  received_t already owns). On ZLINK_RECV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL (ENOBUFS), the returned count is the
  needed size — grow to that and retry; the record is preserved so the retry gets the same record.
  Prefer reusing an existing per-socket/per-received buffer to keep this zero/low-alloc.
- Preserve the exact public parity: same return values for success / non-blocking no-data (EAGAIN) /
  errors; same received_t contents (parts order/bytes, routing id, reply token); same ownership
  (each part closed exactly once — reuse received_t's existing close path). Keep any existing
  single-part fast path if it stays correct.
- native_receive.hpp: add thin wrappers over zlink_recv / zlink_router_recv (mirroring the existing
  recv_part wrappers). Do NOT remove the recv_part wrappers if other code (e.g. the single-part
  recv(message_t&) overload) still uses them — those per-part public overloads stay.
- The raw header mirror bindings/cpp/include/zlink/socket/api.h already has the new declarations
  (synced). Do not edit headers by hand; if a mismatch appears, run
  `python3 scripts/local-package/sync-version.py --check`.

